cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "sensors2heightmap-isaaclab: heightmap reconstruction from LiDAR and depth cameras for vision locomotion policies"
abstract: >-
  An Isaac Lab set of tools for heightmap reconstruction from a LiDAR or a
  depth camera: a network predicts the heightmap of a vision locomotion
  policy from the sensor and the robot's proprioception, so the policy runs
  on the robot without a height scanner.
authors:
  - given-names: Valerio
    family-names: Belli
    email: valerio.belli@iit.it
    affiliation: "Istituto Italiano di Tecnologia (IIT)"
repository-code: "https://github.com/iit-DLSLab/sensors2heightmap-isaaclab"
license: BSD-3-Clause
keywords:
  - legged robots
  - heightmap reconstruction
  - lidar
  - depth camera
  - Isaac Lab
  - reinforcement learning
